			Directories
			-----------


When you unpack a distribution you get several directories. Here is a
list, with a summary of what is found in each.

	actiff
		The actiff library for manipulating TIFF files.

	apilib
		Source for the API library.

	call
		A place to build the call control libraries needed
		for some test programs

	diag
		Source for tools used for test and diagnostics.
		These may use unpublished API calls, and should not
		be copied for application code, since any unpublished
		API calls maye be changed or removed without notice.

	faxlib
		The fax library.

	faxtest
		Source for test programs which use fax. They can also
		be used as examples.

	highapi
		The high-level API libraries and header files

	hsif
		Internal interface definitions for communication
		between host and running firmware (Host/Sharc InterFace).

	libutil
		Source used by code in other directories.

	notes
		Documentation.

	switch
		A place to build the switch libraries needed
		for some test programs

	test
		Source for various test programs. These use the published
		API, so they can be used as examples of how to write
		applications.

	util
		Pre-built utility to download firmware kernel and
		install/uninstall device drivers.

In addition, there are directory names that are used in many places.
These are:

	SOL
		Files for Solaris only.

	SOL_WS
		Files for Solaris with Workshop compiler (now Forte)

	WINNT
		Files for Windows NT only.

	gen
		Files which are generated automatically.

	gen-SOL
		Solaris-specific files which are generated automatically
		(including those supplied pre-built).

	gen-SOL_WS
		Solaris-specific files built by or used with the Workshop
		compiler which are generated automatically
		(including those supplied pre-built).

	gen-WINNT
		Windows NT-specific files which are generated
		automatically (including those suppliled pre-built).

	errs
		Errors, warnings, and other output recorded while
		attempting to generate output files. When building any
		file, f, the errors are recorded in errs/f (where the
		name 'f' can include directories). For example, when
		compiling gen-SOL/test.o any errors get recorded in
		errs/gen-SOL/test.o. A separate errors file is used for
		each generated file to avoid discarding errors from one
		file while building others.
